# about -- the program a person on this disk uses to ask what something is
# and how to run it.  Two defects were found in it on 2026-09-02 and both
# are asserted here.
#
# 1. IT PRINTED NO HOW-TO LINE AT ALL.  `tools/howto.psv' has carried
#    measured invocations for months and gen_catalog wraps each one under
#    the program's entry in DOC/CATEGORIES -- and `about' read that file for
#    the CATEGORY and stopped.  So the single most useful thing the
#    collection knows about a program never reached the person asking.
#
# 2. IT SAID `not here' FOR PATHS THAT ARE HERE.  It re-derived the answer
#    rather than trusting DOC/DEPENDS, and its probe was built only for a
#    lowercase `/dd/' or `/h0/' prefix.  The TeX binaries carry their paths
#    in UPPER CASE, so `about virmf' reported twenty-one directories missing
#    -- including SYS/TEX/MFINPUTS and the two Metafont bases that now ship.
#    DOC/DEPENDS had them right the whole time.

family  about

setup   export TERM=vt100

case    about-prints-the-how-to-line
run     /dd/CMDS/about yagi
expect  Yagi antenna design calculator, to DL6WU's method
expect  for        SYSTEM & MODULES -- Utilities
expect  how        It asks FIVE questions on standard input
expect  run it     yagi
expect  take it    keep yagi

case    about-reports-an-UPPERCASE-path-that-is-here-as-here
run     /dd/CMDS/about virmf
expect  /DD/SYS/TEX/FONTS                      here
expect  /DD/SYS/TEX/MFBASES                    here
expect  /DD/SYS/TEX/MFINPUTS                   here
expect  /DD/USR/TEX/MFBASES                    not here

case    about-still-says-not-here-for-what-is-genuinely-absent
# The fix must not turn the column into a rubber stamp: /DD/USR/... is not
# on this disk and must still read `not here'.
run     /dd/CMDS/about virmf
expect  /DD/USR/TEX/FONTS                      not here
expect  /DD/USR/TEX/BIB                        not here
expect  /DD/SYS/TEX/MFINPUTS/LOCAL             not here

case    about-on-a-program-with-source-and-documentation
run     /dd/CMDS/about fortune
expect  fortune        print a random quotation
expect  for        TEXT TOOLS -- Fortune & sayings
expect  from       Usenet           fortune.ar
expect  needs      /dd/GAMES/FORTUNE/fortunes.dat         here
expect  source     SRC/fortune
expect  run it     fortune

case    about-says-so-when-it-does-not-know-the-name
run     /dd/CMDS/about zzznosuchprogram
expect  zzznosuchprogram: not in DOC/INDEX on /dd
